<title>MEXICO: ICA undertaking $28 million in projects.</title>
<headline>ICA undertaking $28 million in projects.</headline>
<dateline>MONTERREY, Mexico 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Construction company Empresas ICA Sociedad Controladora SA de CV will undertake two heavy construction projects in Guatemala and Mexico worth about $28 million, the company said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>In Guatemala, the company is repairing two stretches of highway CA-10, in a project worth about $14 million.</p>
<p>In Mexico, it was awarded a $14 million contract for work on part of the Mexicali-Tijuana highway.</p>
<p>((--Monterrey newsroom +528 345 7617))</p>
